<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Hex Blocks is a game for one player. Pieces made of four hexagons fall into a well shaped like a honeycomb. Turn each piece and slide it left or right as it falls. When a zigzag row is full from side to side, it disappears. The game ends when the pieces reach the top."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_keyboard}>{dgettext("help_games", "Controls")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The left and right arrows")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Move the piece left or right. Keep the arrow pressed to keep moving"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The up arrow or X, and Z")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Turn the piece one way or the other. Next to a wall, the piece moves aside to turn"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The down arrow")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Hold it to make the piece fall faster"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The space bar")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Drop the piece to the bottom at once. Its shadow in the well shows where it will land"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "C or %{shift}", shift: "Shift")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Save the piece for later and take the next one. You can do this once for each piece"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "On a phone")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Tap the buttons under the well. You can hold a move with one thumb and turn with the other"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_games", "Rules")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "When a piece lands on the pile, you have half a second to slide it into a gap before it stays there."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "The next three pieces are shown beside the well. Every ten pieces, each of the ten shapes comes once."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "Hex Blocks is the Marathon: every ten rows the level goes up and the pieces fall faster. Hex Blocks: Sprint is 40 rows against the clock, and the speed never changes."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_games", "Score")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "In the Marathon, rows cleared together are worth more: 100, 300, 600 or 1,000 points, multiplied by the level. Clearing rows with several pieces in a row adds a bonus. Making a piece fall faster, or dropping it, also adds points."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "In the Sprint, only your time counts: 40 rows in 30 seconds score 10,000, and a slower time scores less. If the pile reaches the top first, it scores nothing."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_joystick}>{dgettext("help_games", "Inspiration")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Games of falling blocks have been loved since the 1980s. Hex Blocks is played on a honeycomb, so its pieces are made of hexagons and each row is a zigzag."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_games", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-hex-sudoku">{dgettext("help_games", "Hex Sudoku")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-retro-games">{dgettext("help_games", "Retro Games")}</.help_link>
</p>
